A main-thread command that assigns a double-quoted dollar-parenthesis command substitution, which appends to the top-level .gitignore of the sandbox repo, must be DENIED. The append runs inside a substitution nested in double quotes, so the guard must scan the substitution body even though the quotes wrap it. Pinned as a characterization case: the guard already denies this shape, so the expected result is a deny JSON on stdout.
